From 7aa82e5f993bce24e84095d0b2895bab9c3351a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Isaac Duarte <31712685+Isaac-Duarte@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:35:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: keep the ATC usb-aon power
 domains on

On the J714s both Type-C ports are dead after a suspend-to-idle wake.
The PHY's first start after it times out in its first power-up step:

  apple-t6050-dp-phy 2ab000000.phy: start of mode 1 failed (-110)
  apple-t6050-dp-phy 383000000.phy: CIO mode failed (-110), reverse orientation, 1 ms

Traced with pmgr-pwrstate's dynamic debug: at the noirq suspend genpd
gates each port's usb domain, which was off at probe and so has no
GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP, and with it its parents, common and usb-aon,
whose own devices (the display crossbar's and the PHY's) have suspended.
Nothing sets the PHY up again at an s2idle wake.

DjDeveloperr noted that the usb-aon domains should not be turned off
("aon = always on"). The older SoCs (T8103, T8112, T600x, T602x) and
T604x mark them apple,always-on; T603x, T8122, T8140 and T8132 outside
the J713 do not, and neither did T6050.

Tested on the J714s: with only atc0/1/2's usb-aon marked always-on and a
PHY driver without any s2idle handling, genpd still gated atc*_usb and
atc*_common on all three ports during a 42 s s2idle and powered them on
again at the resume, but never touched usb-aon. After the wake a dock on
the right port came up in CIO mode at the first plug, with three
displays. With this patch's DTB, three s2idle sleeps in one boot (39 s,
102 s and 12 min) were each followed by a dock coming up in CIO mode at
the first plug on all three ports. Keeping usb-aon on is enough; gating
usb and common across s2idle is harmless.

Mark every T6050 usb-aon domain always-on. At runtime nothing changes
where the display crossbar holds the domain from its probe on, as on the
J714s (atc1, atc2) and the J716c (atc0 to atc2). On the other T6050
boards the crossbar is disabled, so a usb-aon domain used by a PHY went
off while its port was idle and now stays on (J714c, J716s, K114c,
K116s: atc1, atc2; J775c, J873s: atc1, atc3; J775d: atc1, atc3, atc4,
atc5), and an enabled usb-aon domain with no user is now powered at
probe (atc3 on the J714c, J716c, J716s, K114c, K114s, K116c and K116s;
atc1 on the K114s and K116c). The idle power this costs there, and the
PHY without a usb-aon power cycle on those boards, are untested. genpd
no longer gates usb-aon in a deep sleep's noirq phase either; the J714s
already keeps ATC3's on through the commit (t6050-j714s-sleep.dtsi), and
deep sleep cannot run on the J714s today, so that part is untested.

Signed-off-by: Isaac Duarte <31712685+Isaac-Duarte@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi        | 2 ++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-dieX.dtsi        | 1 +
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-peripherals.dtsi | 1 +
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-ultra.dtsi       | 1 +
 4 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi
index fdd2f6bfa746..caa23251d0f9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-die0.dtsi
@@ -998,6 +998,7 @@ ps_atc2_usb_aon: power-controller@178 {
 		compatible = "apple,t6050-pmgr-pwrstate", "apple,t8103-pmgr-pwrstate";
 		reg = <0x178 4>;
 		label = "atc2_usb_aon";
+		apple,always-on; /* The ATC PHY loses its state without it */
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 		#reset-cells = <0>;
 		status = "disabled";
@@ -1029,6 +1030,7 @@ ps_atc3_usb_aon: power-controller@190 {
 		compatible = "apple,t6050-pmgr-pwrstate", "apple,t8103-pmgr-pwrstate";
 		reg = <0x190 4>;
 		label = "atc3_usb_aon";
+		apple,always-on; /* The ATC PHY loses its state without it */
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 		#reset-cells = <0>;
 	};
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-dieX.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-dieX.dtsi
index 94e9def5533f..6c6a48ca205c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-dieX.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-dieX.dtsi
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ DIE_NODE(ps_atc1_usb_aon): power-controller@160 {
 			compatible = "apple,t6050-pmgr-pwrstate", "apple,t8103-pmgr-pwrstate";
 			reg = <0x160 4>;
 			label = DIE_ATC1_LABEL(_usb_aon);
+			apple,always-on; /* The ATC PHY loses its state without it */
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 			#reset-cells = <0>;
 		};
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-peripherals.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-peripherals.dtsi
index 5c4a029f5751..ee04965ce117 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-peripherals.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-peripherals.dtsi
@@ -931,6 +931,7 @@ ps_atc0_usb_aon: power-controller@148 {
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 		#reset-cells = <0>;
 		label = "atc0-usb-aon";
+		apple,always-on; /* The ATC PHY loses its state without it */
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
 	ps_atc0_usb: power-controller@150 {
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-ultra.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-ultra.dtsi
index fae5621266fb..90bf4bb29be0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-ultra.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-ultra.dtsi
@@ -120,6 +120,7 @@ ps_atc4_usb_aon: power-controller@148 {
 		compatible = "apple,t6050-pmgr-pwrstate", "apple,t8103-pmgr-pwrstate";
 		reg = <0x148 4>;
 		label = "atc4_usb_aon";
+		apple,always-on; /* The ATC PHY loses its state without it */
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 		#reset-cells = <0>;
 	};
